==Battleground==
*10 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 3~13.33 seconds<sup>90f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 4~10 seconds<sup>120f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 16.67~26.67 seconds<sup>500f~800f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 4~13.33 seconds<sup>120f~400f</sup>.
**100 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.07~2 seconds<sup>2f~60f</sup>.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] spawns.
**1 [[St. Pigge the 2nd]] spawns.
**5 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
If you own [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier]] and [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]], the stage becomes a cakewalk, only the 2,200% Nyandam serving some trouble.

Otherwise, bring meatshields along with [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] to create a dense frontline defense. Cameraman can deal extra damage to the horde of Shy Boys that come in and may try to push through your meatshields and Cameraman stacks. Carry [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon]], and [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]] as your backliners if you own them.
[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] is highly recommended as it can survive a hit from Nyandam and has impressive stats against the Red enemies here.
Lastly, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]] can be great for clearing the waves of Ginger Snaches and any enemies hiding back.

